"Objects": 
    [
        {
            'Key': 'foo',
            'Attribute1': 'something',
            'Attribute2': 'something else'
        },
        {
            // ...
        }
    ]
}
</code></pre> <p>{% hint style="info" %} * An input object MUST contain an attribute "Key", with the value being a unique key identifying this object in the ADAL table.  * There must not be any duplicate objects (i.e. having the same key) in the input array.</p> <p>Failing either one of these criteria will result in the failure of the entire operation. {% endhint %}</p> <p>BatchPut outputs an array of ImportedObject matching with the input array. This means that output.ImportedObjects[x] is an ImportedObject describing the operation result of the object input.Objects[x]. The status of a returned ImportedObject can only be "Inserted" or "Error".</p>

